# start Validation Reply Form
_vrf_PLAT250_(S2MeBA)2PbI4_100K_quench
;
PROBLEM: Large U3/U1 Ratio for Average U(i,j) Tensor ....        4.2 Note
RESPONSE: Due to the thermal motion and vibration of the organic cation, the displacement ellipsoids are not ideally shaped, but the atom-type assignment is correct and the organic cation carbon and nitrogen atom positions are unambiguously determined.
;
_vrf_PLAT342_(S2MeBA)2PbI4_100K_quench
;
PROBLEM: Low Bond Precision on  C-C Bonds ...............    0.02837 Ang.
RESPONSE: This problem is due to the thermal motion of the carbon atoms. Since we mainly focus on the analysis of the inorganic component of the structure, this alert involving organic cation will not affect our study.
;
_vrf_PLAT971_(S2MeBA)2PbI4_100K_quench
;
PROBLEM: Check Calcd Resid. Dens.  1.61Ang From I3              2.87 eA-3
RESPONSE: This alert is due to the excess electron density near the heavy atoms, which is not from unaccounted atom types. This excess residual density is ~5% of the assigned q peak and may be considered within experimental error (and possibly related to strongly absorbing nature of the crystal and the associated absorption correction). Such alert doesn't impact the structure solution. 
;
_vrf_PLAT971_(S2MeBA)2PbI4_100K_quench_2
;
PROBLEM: Check Calcd Resid. Dens.  1.71Ang From I2              2.71 eA-3
RESPONSE: This alert is due to the excess electron density near the heavy atoms, which is not from unaccounted atom types. This excess residual density is ~5% of the assigned q peak and may be considered within experimental error (and possibly related to strongly absorbing nature of the crystal and the associated absorption correction). Such alert doesn't impact the structure solution. 
;
_vrf_PLAT973_(S2MeBA)2PbI4_100K_quench
;
PROBLEM: Check Calcd Positive Resid. Density on        Pb       1.78 eA-3
RESPONSE: This alert is due to the excess electron density near the heavy atoms, which is not from unaccounted atom types. This excess residual density is ~5% of the assigned q peak and may be considered within experimental error (and possibly related to strongly absorbing nature of the crystal and the associated absorption correction). Such alert doesn't impact the structure solution.
;
